<ul>
  <li>Workspace never replaces an item silently. When you choose <b>Replace</b>, the old item is kept beside the new one, named “Workspace replaced item…”, until you remove it. Folders are replaced, never merged.</li>
  <li>A copy is written somewhere private first and only appears when it is complete, so a stopped or failed copy never leaves half a file behind.</li>
  <li>Moving to another disk copies first, checks the copy, and only then removes the original. If anything changed in the meantime, the original is kept and Workspace tells you where.</li>
  <li>When something can't be done, one message lists each item and the reason. When everything works, Workspace says nothing.</li>
</ul>
